mm6108-driver (2.1.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/patches/fix-linux-7.0-build.patch: fix the build against Linux
    7.0. Upstream selects the ieee80211_mgmt action-frame layout and the
    wireless_dev get_station() signature from 7.0, but both first appeared
    in 7.1-rc1.

 -- Austin <vidplace7@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

mm6108-driver (2.1.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/mm6108-driver-dkms.dkms: pass KERNEL_SRC. Upstream's Makefile
    adds '-I$(KERNEL_SRC)' right before '-DCONFIG_MORSE_SDIO'; with
    KERNEL_SRC unset the bare '-I' consumed that define, so the SDIO bus
    driver was never registered.
  * debian/mm6108-driver-dkms.dkms: build with CONFIG_MORSE_SDIO_ALIGNMENT=4
    so bulk SDIO buffers meet the 4-byte DMA alignment required by common
    SBC MMC hosts (sunxi-mmc, dw_mmc, meson-gx-mmc); upstream defaults to 2.
  * debian/mm6108-driver-dkms.dkms: build with CONFIG_MORSE_COUNTRY=US to
    default the 'country' module parameter to US instead of upstream's AU.
  * debian/mm6108-driver-dkms.dkms: build with CONFIG_MORSE_POWERSAVE_MODE=0
    to disable power save by default (the 'enable_ps' module parameter);
    upstream defaults to fully enabled.
  * Mark Morse Micro interfaces unmanaged by NetworkManager. NetworkManager
    claims them as ordinary Wi-Fi and hands them to the stock wpa_supplicant,
    which has no S1G support, while randomising the MAC on every scan; it has
    no way to drive the S1G supplicant because it hardcodes the D-Bus name
    fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1. Ships
    /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/90-morse-nm-unmanaged.rules, setting NM_UNMANAGED=1
    for the morse_usb, morse_sdio and morse_spi drivers. This is the
    mechanism NetworkManager documents for the purpose and only sets a
    default: 'nmcli device set <iface> managed yes' still overrides it, which
    would not be true of an unmanaged-devices entry in NetworkManager.conf.

 -- Austin <vidplace7@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

mm6108-driver (2.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release (upstream tag mm6108-2.1.1).
  * debian/watch: track the per-chip 'mm6108-' tags; upstream now tags the
    MM6108 and MM8108 series separately.
  * debian/watch: match the archive extension in filenamemangle so the
    downloaded tarball is not named mm6108-driver-<version>.tar.gz.tar.gz.
  * debian/rules: clone the 'mm6108-<upstream version>' tag in
    get-orig-source, derived from the changelog version.
  * debian/copyright: declare the upstream license as GPL-2.0-or-later to
    match the SPDX headers in the upstream sources, and extend the copyright
    years to 2026.

 -- Austin <vidplace7@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

mm6108-driver (1.17.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split morse-driver into per-chip packages; this is the MM6108 variant.
  * Rename source package to mm6108-driver and binary package to
    mm6108-driver-dkms.
  * Rename the DKMS module tree to /usr/src/mm6108-driver-<version>.
  * Recommend mm6108-firmware instead of morse-firmware.
  * Conflict with mm8108-driver-dkms; the two chip variants are mutually
    exclusive.

